{"id":"three-count","name":"Three count","chapter":"Tricks in three count / causal diagrams","kind":"pattern","page":20,"label":"19","jugglers":2,"objects":null,"timing":null,"pdf":"https://www.jugglingedge.com/pdf/highgate.pdf#page=20&view=FitH,741","passist":"https://alpha.passist.org/extended-siteswap/(2,4x)(4x,2)/(2,4x)(4x,2)","passist_candidate":"https://alpha.passist.org/extended-siteswap/(2,4x)(4x,2)/(2,4x)(4x,2)","p4ssist":{"url":"https://pass.algrant.ca/siteswap/24b.4a2.24d.4c2?jugglers=2","kind":"sync","names":["A","B"]},"notations":[],"derived":{"kind":"prechac","value":"3p 3 3","global":null,"confidence":"low","matches_stated":null,"sync":{"per_juggler":{"A":"(2,4x)*","B":"(2,4x)*"},"drawn":{"A":"(2,4xp)(4x,2)(2,4x)","B":"(2,4xp)(4x,2)(2,4x)"}}},"body":[{"t":"p","h":"Causal diagrams show how one throw causes another throw. In three count both jugglers start with a right handed pass. In order to catch Anne&#x27;s pass, Ben has to throw the club he&#x27;s holding in his left hand. So Anne&#x27;s first right hand throw causes Ben&#x27;s first left hand throw. This is shown by drawing an arrow from Anne&#x27;s first right hand beat to Ben&#x27;s first left hand beat."},{"t":"d","i":0},{"t":"p","h":"Ben throws a right hand pass at the same time as Anne. This pass causes Anne&#x27;s first left hand throw. This is shown by drawing an arrow from Ben&#x27;s first right hand beat to Anne&#x27;s first left hand beat."},{"t":"d","i":1},{"t":"p","h":"Anne&#x27;s first left hand throw is a self. In order to catch this self she has to throw the club she&#x27;s holding in her right hand. So her first left hand throw causes her second right hand throw. This is shown by drawing an arrow from Anne&#x27;s first left hand beat to her second right hand beat."},{"t":"d","i":2},{"t":"p","h":"Ben throws a left hand self at the same time as Anne. This self causes his second right hand throw. This is shown by drawing an arrow from Ben&#x27;s first left hand beat to his second right hand beat."},{"t":"d","i":3},{"t":"p","h":"For both jugglers the third throw is a right hand self, which causes the next left hand throw. The fourth throw is a left hand pass which causes the other juggler to do a right hand throw. The fifth throw is a right hand self which causes a left hand throw. The sixth throw is a left hand self which causes the next right hand throw. The pattern then repeats."},{"t":"d","i":4},{"t":"p","h":"I often scribble causal diagrams on bits of paper and I find that drawing all the arrow heads takes time and makes the diagram look ugly, so I leave them out! If a line in a causal diagram has no arrow head then you can assume that the arrow is pointing towards the right of the diagram."},{"t":"d","i":5},{"t":"p","h":"Causal diagrams assume that each hand is holding a club. Also each line represents a club in the air. As there are four hands, and two line running through this pattern, this diagram shows a six club pattern. Apart from some beats at the beginning and end of the diagram, each beat has one arrow pointing to it and one arrow pointing away from it. In this diagram each juggler&#x27;s first right hand beat has no arrow pointing to it. This shows that both jugglers start with an extra club in their right hand."}],"drawings":[{"file":"p20-1.png","kind":"causal diagram","reading":{"rows":[{"juggler":"A","name":"Anne","offset":0.0,"tempo":1.0,"beats":[{"t":0.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":1.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":2.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":3.0,"hand":"L"}]},{"juggler":"B","name":"Ben","offset":0.0,"tempo":1.0,"beats":[{"t":0.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":1.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":2.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":3.0,"hand":"L"}]}],"arrows":[{"from":[0,0.0,"R"],"to":[1,1.0,"L"],"grey":true,"head":true}],"holds":"unlinked","sync":false,"grid":2,"unit_px":63.0,"layout":{"x0":130.0,"unit":63.0,"rows_y":[27.0,90.0],"names":[[8,9,97,38,"Anne"],[33,72,97,101,"Ben"]],"dots":[]},"tempos":[1.0],"names":["Anne","Ben"],"n_nodes":8,"leftover_px":0,"unlinked":6},"orig":"orig/p20-1.png"},{"file"